## What this session did

Landed **P0/P1 of the sess102 RULE-5 ruling** — the top open defect's blocking step. `0.11.436`, builds clean (srcversion `17AC8BF7EEB583CC1A36405`), **not deployed, not measured**.

The authority token was being resolved in `xfs_buf_item_format_segment` at CIL format time. That is unsound: a format-time lookup reports whichever grant is installed when the CIL runs, not the grant that authorized the mutation (`modify under E1 → release → reacquire E2 → format stamps E2` emits a false token). Capture now happens at `xfs_trans_dirty_buf` — the single seam every buffer passes through to become dirty, where the transaction still holds the authorizing tenure — and the formatter only serializes it. Five files; this also closes the "RULING ITEM (b) — still owed" comment that two independent consults had converged on.

Two things that would have silently broken it, both verified in source first:

- The window key can't be the `tp` pointer (slab reuse would alias a fresh transaction and suppress the recapture — precisely the stale stamp being fixed). Added `t_mxfs_capseq`, lazily assigned; `kmem_cache_zalloc` in both `xfs_trans_alloc` and `xfs_trans_dup` zeroes it, so a rolled transaction correctly opens a new window.
- `__bli_format` carries the BLFT for every buffer but `blf_blkno` only for single-map ones. Taking both from one `blfp` would have classified every discontiguous buffer into AG 0.

Also confirmed by exhaustive grep that nothing consumes these tokens yet (`mxfs_auth_st_proves` and the INODE/ICLUS classes have zero callers), so the landing cannot change an apply/skip decision — only what gets stamped.

Shipped the instrument the ruling demanded, `P240-AUTHCAP`, including the decisive `outcome × (dlm_mode ≥ PW)` cross-tab that separates "the recorder is broken" from "genuinely unauthorized modification", plus `nocap` (must be 0), `mismatch` (the one-buffer-two-authorities case, downgraded to MIXED rather than overwritten), and `noblft` (measures the design's one unproven assumption: that `xfs_trans_buf_set_type` always precedes the first dirty). Report trigger moved to the capture path at 1023, fixing the sess102 finding that the old 8192 modulus sampled one node rather than the fleet.

